decision: changes-requested

Previous findings are accounted for below: R5-N16, R6-N17 and R6-N18 remain partial; R6-N19 is fixed.

Four high-severity blockers remain:

- **R7-N20:** The symlink scan skips submodule contents, allowing declared dependency aliases inside gitlinks to retain stale passes. Gitlinks reference separate repositories’ commits. [Git documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitsubmodules.html)
- **R7-N21:** `material_clean` ignores untracked inputs created during validation.
- **R7-N22:** The case-sensitivity probe examines only the root directory. Linux permits case-sensitive and case-folded directories within one filesystem. [Kernel documentation](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/ext4.html)
- **R7-N23:** Git configuration can hide changed gitlinks. I reproduced this with the existing regression test under `diff.ignoreSubmodules=all`: validation selected zero modules and reported SUCCESS. [Git documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-diff)

Targeted tests, race tests, build and vet passed. Both strict validation commands exited 1; repository-wide validation reported 235/236 passing. The broader `internal/pose` test run timed out. The sealed canonical results remain historical green evidence, not a fresh local pass. No repository changes or attestation were made.

